{"type":"message","id":"d676c2c8","parentId":"9c857f81","timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:47:26.640Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py`. It now uses `datetime.fromisoformat(s)` instead of `strptime` with a fixed format. On Python 3.13, `fromisoformat` accepts the trailing `Z` and reads it as UTC. All 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` pass.\n\nTwo changes in behaviour you should know about:\n- **Inputs ending in `Z` now come back timezone-aware:** `parse_date(\"2026-10-12T08:30:00Z\")` returns a datetime with `tzinfo=timezone.utc`. Inputs without `Z` still come back with no timezone, so `\"2026-01-02T03:04:05\"` is unchanged. The only other caller in the repo is `day_key`, which only formats the date, so it isn't affected. But code outside this repo that compares or subtracts a `Z` result against a datetime with no timezone will now raise `TypeError`.\n- **More formats are accepted:** `parse_date` now also takes things like date-only strings, fractional seconds and offsets such as `+02:00`. Before, those raised `ValueError`.\n\nThe repo doesn't pin a Python version. `fromisoformat` only accepts `Z` on Python 3.11 and later, so on anything older the original error comes back."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":428,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":27496,"totalTokens":27926,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":27496}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792277242201,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg8d6Uqmg4Cn9JVBmab4u","duration":4438.014493999999,"ttft":4414.180780999999,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":27498,"nonMessageTokens":21589,"compactionEpoch":0}}}
